# The repo-root .gitignore has a blanket `*.log` rule, which silently swallows
# every fixture in this directory — they are captured `swift test` output and
# `.log` is what they are. Re-include them here rather than renaming: an
# ignored fixture is not a missing file you notice, it is a corpus that quietly
# stops containing its own test cases, which reads as a pass.
#
# swift-suite_test.sh additionally asserts each fixture is tracked, so a new
# one added under a pattern this does not cover fails loudly instead of
# disappearing.
!*.log
